 "tr_note": "The Textus Receptus reads ἔκραζον, 'were crying out', for ἐκραύγασαν, 'cried out'; the YLT's 'were crying out' matches it, while the KJV's 'cried out' does not show the tense. It reads αὐτόν for ἑαυτόν, 'himself', yet the KJV still has 'himself'. It has ἐζήτει, 'was seeking', at another place in the sentence, which is the KJV's 'Pilate sought'."
